# client-custom-fields.declared-limit.must-fail.patch
#
# Targets: AC-33 (the collection's declared unpaged default — `limit: 0` —
# reaches the wire on the first request; legacy parity, `customFields.vue:261-272`) —
# client-custom-fields.criteria-defaults.int.test.ts:89-101, the
# "AC-33 asks for the whole catalogue by default — limit=0 on the first
# request" case.
#
# Authored by: developer seat (agent-seat-separation.companion.md — the seat
# that knows the exact line it changed authors the mutant; the prover applies
# it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to construct it).
#
# REBASED (2026-08-22, developer seat, factory run) — the prior hunk's
# context line read `offset: { type: "integer", minimum: 0 }`. This run
# landed a `pagination.offset` default (`client-custom-fields.schemas.ts:113`
# now reads `offset: { type: "integer", minimum: 0, default: 0 }`), so that
# unchanged context line no longer matches the tree and `git apply` refuses
# the hunk. This rebase updates ONLY the context line to the new offset
# declaration; the mutated line is unchanged and still targets `limit`
# alone — a sibling control already covers the offset default, so this
# control stays scoped to `limit` to keep the two distinct.
#
# Mutates: client-custom-fields.schemas.ts — `useQuerySchema()`'s
# `pagination.limit.default` from `0` to `10`, the exact value
# `withPageWindow`'s own `PAGINATION.limit` (`query.utils.ts:71`) would
# supply if this module declared no default at all (`design.md`, "the
# mechanism this design relies on").
#
# Expected RED: the declared default no longer beats `withPageWindow`'s own
# `PAGINATION.limit` merge distinctly — `useQuerySchema()`'s own
# `pagination.limit.default` reads `10`, so a fresh boot's first request
# carries `limit=10`. AC-33's read-back
# (`observed.first().url.searchParams.get("limit") === "0"`, i.e.
# `params.get("limit")` deep-equal to `DECLARED_LIMIT` in
# client-custom-fields.criteria-defaults.int.test.ts) goes RED.
#
# Apply / verify / revert:
#   git apply <this file>     # mutate
#   pnpm test client-custom-fields.criteria-defaults.int.test.ts    # must go RED
#   git apply -R <this file>  # revert — must return to green
#
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/client-custom-fields.schemas.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/client-custom-fields.schemas.ts
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
         // `minimum: 0`, not 1: `limit: 0` stays legal — this module's own
         // unpaged default (legacy parity, see the docblock above).
         properties: {
-          limit: { type: "integer", minimum: 0, default: 0 },
+          limit: { type: "integer", minimum: 0, default: 10 },
           offset: { type: "integer", minimum: 0, default: 0 }
         }
       }
